# Backend runtime only. Supply real values through your server's secret store.
# Never expose these values in VITE_* variables, browser bundles, or API responses.
# Protected API routes require this key in the X-Api-Key header.
INTERNAL_API_KEY=

# Optional Google Apps Script deployments for the public website forms.
# Leave blank to disable delivery: the matching endpoint responds 503 {"ok":false}.
# There are no fallback deployment URLs. Configure each deployment explicitly.
# Required URL shape: https://script.google.com/macros/s/<deployment-id>/exec
# HTTPS only; no credentials, query string, fragment, or nonstandard port.
GOOGLE_CONTACT_SCRIPT_URL=
GOOGLE_NEWSLETTER_SCRIPT_URL=

# Public routes (no INTERNAL_API_KEY required ONLY for these exact POST paths):
# POST /api/submit-contact
# POST /api/newsletter-track
# Existing OPTIONS handling is unchanged. Other methods and trailing-slash or
# prefix variants are not exempt from authentication.
#
# Forms require Content-Type: application/json and an object body <= 32768 bytes,
# including streamed bodies. Invalid JSON/fields return 400, oversize bodies 413,
# and unsupported content types 415. Error responses contain {"ok":false}.
# Contact accepts only name, email, organization, message. All are strings and
# are trimmed. Name, email, and message are required; organization is optional.
# Character limits: name 200, email 254, organization 200, message 8000.
# Newsletter reason must be an integer 1..5, or a whole integer string in that
# range. It is forwarded as an integer; other finite JSON metadata is preserved.
#
# Delivery sends personal data to the configured Google deployment. Review its
# access, retention, privacy notice, and quotas before enabling production.
# A final upstream 2xx returns 200 {"ok":true}; other upstream statuses, transport
# failures, and timeouts return 502, never a fake success or the upstream body.
# Delivery has a 15-second overall deadline, 3-second connect/pool timeouts,
# 10-second read/write timeouts, and at most three HTTPS redirects within
# script.google.com / script.googleusercontent.com. Redirects never replay POST
# bodies; initial 307/308 responses fail closed. Responses are not cached.
#
# Production must enforce rate limits and spam/bot controls at the reverse proxy
# or WAF. Apply per-client limits, the body cap, and inbound read timeouts before
# proxying these public forms. Trust forwarded client IPs only from your proxy.
# CORS is not spam protection. Do not log request bodies, deployment URLs, or keys.
# No distributed rate limiter or CAPTCHA service is configured by this backend.
#
# Vite/nginx integration: route the exact public form POST paths to this backend.
# /api/backend/* aliases are deliberately NOT exposed by FastAPI. The server-side
# proxy must allow only GET requests to the exact public paths used by lib/api.ts,
# strip /api/backend while preserving the remaining path, trailing slash, and
# query string, and overwrite X-Api-Key with the backend INTERNAL_API_KEY value.
# Never accept a browser-provided key or put it in a URL. Preserve upstream error
# statuses, Content-Type, Content-Disposition, and Cache-Control for exports.
# Never expose a catch-all keyed proxy, /api/v1/data-files/*, or admin operations.
# Keep the backend private behind that proxy where practical. Existing API key
# checks on /api/v1/* remain enabled, including public-data GET routes.
